Sure! To update a break node’s label to `"loopEnd"` (but only if it isn’t already `"loopEnd"`), you can use the `updateBreak` function.  
Just provide the node you want to update (in string form) and the new label. Here’s how you’d call it:

```javascript
// Replace the placeholder with your actual node string
const nodeString = /* your break node as a string */;

// Call the function
const result = updateBreak({
  node: nodeString,
  label: "loopEnd"
});

console.log(result);
```

If you paste the actual node string into `nodeString`, the function will check the current label and replace it with `"loopEnd"` only when necessary. Let me know if you need help formatting the node string or anything else!
